@startuml

title Report processing: the two chains a run configuration can build

participant "workflow engine" as wf
participant "pre-processing" as pre
participant "compute" as comp
participant "post-processing" as post
participant "ores.storage" as store

== Execute both ends: the full chain ==
wf -> pre : reporting.v1.ops.preprocess
pre -> store : generate and store reporting/inputs/{digest}.tar.gz
pre --> wf : input location and digest
wf -> comp : compute.v1.report.submit
comp --> wf : batch
wf -> post : reporting.v1.ops.postprocess
post -> store : GET the output archive
post --> wf : rows loaded

== Substitute both ends: the chain used while dependencies are missing ==
wf -> pre : reporting.v1.ops.use-prepared-input\n{archive location from the run configuration}
note right of pre : nothing is read from trading or\nmarket data; nothing is generated
pre -> store : HEAD the prepared archive
store --> pre : the location and its digest
pre --> wf : input location and digest
wf -> comp : compute.v1.report.submit
note over wf, comp : the same command, the same payload shape.\nSubmission cannot tell which chain it is in.
comp --> wf : batch
wf -> post : reporting.v1.ops.ignore-results
note right of post : the output location is recorded,\nnothing is fetched or loaded
post --> wf : output location recorded

== The invariant ==
note over wf, comp
  In both chains the four phases that are never substituted
  are identical: submission, execution, retrieval and
  finalisation. A substitute changes what produced the input
  and what consumes the output, and nothing else.
end note

@enduml
